                                            {
                                                "box": {
                                                    "id": "obj-64",
                                                    "maxclass": "newobj",
                                                    "numinlets": 4,
                                                    "numoutlets": 1,
                                                    "outlettype": [ "signal" ],
                                                    "patching_rect": [ 235.0, 461.0, 187.0, 22.0 ],
                                                    "text": "evi.biquad.lowpass~"
                                                }
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "box": {
                                                    "id": "obj-63",
                                                    "linecount": 10,
                                                    "maxclass": "comment",
                                                    "numinlets": 1,
                                                    "numoutlets": 0,
                                                    "patching_rect": [ 975.0, 205.0, 156.0, 141.0 ],
                                                    "text": "In evieve, all the 'evi.filter.*' objects offer the @smooth attribute (default off), which can optionally smooth those simple mixing gains after the calculations and before the DSP. This is a huge cost saving and also opens up other possibilities."
                                                }
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "box": {
                                                    "id": "obj-62",
                                                    "linecount": 13,
                                                    "maxclass": "comment",
                                                    "numinlets": 1,
                                                    "numoutlets": 0,
                                                    "patching_rect": [ 771.0, 205.0, 187.0, 181.0 ],
                                                    "text": "One of the benefits of the TPT SVF topology is that out of it's 6 coefficients, only 3 of them are actual coefficients, the remaining 3 are simple linear mixing gains, some of which are not required depending on filter type. In the case of the lowpass, only 1 mixing gain is required, which means we can just smooth that AFTER the coefficients calculations, just before the filter core."
                                                }
                                            },
